  <notes>Use vi.useFakeTimers() for debounce testing; advance timer to trigger.

Completed 2026-07-03 (out-of-order per user instruction — dep 039 waived because integration test uses mocked Xrm.WebApi, not a deployed webresource).

Delivered: src/solutions/Notepad/src/__tests__/notepad.integration.test.tsx with 10 test cases covering FR-14/15/16/17/18/19 via mocked Xrm.WebApi and virtual mocks of shared-lib services. All 10 pass; full Notepad suite 112/112 (0 regressions from 102 baseline). Zero @spaarke/auth (NFR-05) and zero BFF calls (NFR-07) verified. TypeScript compiles cleanly (only pre-existing shared-lib ComponentFramework errors surface, unrelated).

Test technique notes (for future authors):
  - jsdom's window.location is non-configurable in this jest version; instead we override at the parseDataParams boundary via globalThis.__NOTEPAD_TEST_LAUNCH_SEARCH__ + a virtual mock of `@spaarke/ui-components/utils`. Cleaner than fighting jsdom.
  - MemoEditor's Ctrl+Enter and blur immediate-save paths need direct .value = "..." (no input event fired). The input pipeline causes Fluent v9's internal state to re-render the controlled Textarea, resetting the DOM value to the prop value. This mirrors the pattern the existing NotepadShell.test.tsx already uses.
  - React 18 attaches onBlur via `focusout` (which bubbles) not `blur` (which doesn't). Blur test dispatches focusout.
  - MemoList switch flush semantics (per handleSelect in NotepadShell.tsx and NotepadShell.test.tsx line 596): flushes updateBody(currentMemo.sprk_memobody, {immediate: true}) — using the LAST-SAVED body, NOT pendingBodyRef. This is documented production behavior; pending unsaved typing is lost on manual switch (user is expected to Ctrl+Enter first).
  - Nav-prop discovery mocked at ../hooks/discoverMemoNavProps module level (no fetch).</notes>

